```

But global fetch timeout via AbortController: I clear the timer after headers arrive, but body reading isn't covered by that timer. Better: keep the timer for the whole operation? Actually the body read could hang. Let me keep an overall timeout using AbortSignal that covers both. I'll set the timer to abort, and clear it after the loop. But I currently clear after headers. Let me instead keep a separate body timeout or just keep clearTimeout until after body read. Simpler: only clear the timer when fully done (after body loop). Let me restructure to clear at end.

